TITLE:: MERange
summary:: Main MERange builder class.
categories:: MusicEngine Library
related:: Classes/MENoteRange, Classes/MENote

DESCRIPTION::
MERange is primarily a range builder class. As such, it contains all the methods needed to create new ranges, including the primary constructor methods used by MENoteRange. MERange is also a subclass of LINK::Classes/SequenceableCollection::. Many fundamental tools for interacting with ranges are defined in this class, which are then inherited by MENoteRange for user interaction. MERange and MENoteRange are collections of MENote objects.

NOTE::
MERange is a private class, meant to separate the logic behind range generation from the public interface provided by MENoteRange. As such, the user should use MENoteRange to generate ranges, and not MERange. All instance methods discussed in this file, and implemented at this level, are inherited by MENoteRange.
::



CLASSMETHODS::



METHOD:: new
Creates a new MERange object. It also works as the primary constructor for MENoteRange.

ARGUMENT:: input
The EMPHASIS::input:: argument may take a LINK::Classes/String:: with the range symbol required (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"Cmaj7"::, EMPHASIS::"Em3P5"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.), or an LINK::Classes/Integer:: size.

NOTE:: The Integer instantiation is mostly meant to be used internally, in conjunction with the LINK::Classes/MERange#*with:: method.
::

numberedList::
## A LINK::Classes/String:: will return a collection of MENote objects based on the provided symbol.
## An LINK::Classes/Integer:: will return an empty MERange object with the same number of slots available as the value provided.
::

returns:: Depending on the EMPHASIS::input:: MERange will return either a collection of MENote objects or an empty MERange object of specified size.

CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F#-7"); // Returns collection of MENote objects
b = MENoteRange.new(40);     // Returns an empty MERange object with 40 available slots
::



METHOD:: with
Creates a new MERange object from a preexisting collection of MENote objects.

ARGUMENT:: symbol
A copy of the MESymbol object stored in MERange.

NOTE:: When a new range is created, the symbol used as EMPHASIS::input:: is stored as a MESymbol object. MENoteRange includes a series of methods for accessing data from this object. By copying this object it is ensured that the symbol data is always accessible, even after the range has been manipulated.
::

ARGUMENT::  ... args
A collection of MENote objects to be used in the new MERange object.

returns:: A new MERange object.



PRIVATE:: extendMidiRange, getMENotes, getOffsets, wrapAndExtend, wrapFirstOctave, getRange



INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: meSymbol



SUBSECTION:: Data retrieval



METHOD:: notes
Returns an Array of MENote objects (not a MENoteRange).

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.notes;
::



SUBSECTION:: Common methods



METHOD:: hash
Returns a unique hash value for the range.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.hash; // An integer value
::



METHOD:: at
Returns MENote object at the specified EMPHASIS::index::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.at(20);   // MENote object at index 20
// Same as:
r[20];
::

copymethod:: SequenceableCollection, -first

copymethod:: SequenceableCollection, -last


METHOD:: size
Returns the size of the collection.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.size; // 43
::


METHOD:: species
Returns name of class. Similar to the CODE::class:: method.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.species; // MENoteRange
r.class;   // MENoteRange
::


METHOD:: add
Adds a new EMPHASIS::item:: to the end of a collection.

CODE::
(
r = MENoteRange.new(4);
a = [
	MENote.new("C", 60, \P1),
	MENote.new("E", 64, \M3),
	MENote.new("G", 67, \P5),
	MENote.new("B", 70, \m7)
];
a.do { |n| r.add(n) };
r;
)
::



METHOD:: put
Puts EMPHASIS::item:: at specified EMPHASIS::index::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20];                           // D4 at index 20
r.put(20, MENote.new("C", 60, \P5)); // New MENote object
r[20];                           // Db4 at index 20
::



SUBSECTION:: Copy methods


METHOD:: copy
Returns a deep copy of the collection.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.copy;

r === c;      // false
r[0] === c[0] // false
::



METHOD:: copyRange
Returns a subrange, from EMPHASIS::start:: to EMPHASIS::end::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.copyRange(10,20);  // Returns subrange from index 10 to 20
// Same as:
r[10..20];
::



METHOD:: copySeries
Returns a series, from EMPHASIS::first:: to EMPHASIS::last::, where EMPHASIS::second:: determines the step.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = r.copySeries(10,2,20); // Returns every second item from first to last
// Same as:
r[10,2..20];
::



SUBSECTION:: Iterators



METHOD:: do
Runs a EMPHASIS::function:: for each iteration over a collection. Inside EMPHASIS::function::, the first argument refers to the item, and the second to the index.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].do({ |n, i| "#% : %".format(i, n).postln }); // Function prints every index and item
::



METHOD:: reverseDo
Same as CODE::do:: but in reverse order.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].reverseDo({ |n, i| "#% : %".format(i, n).postln }); // Function prints every index and item, in reverse
::



METHOD:: select
Returns a new collection with every item for which the EMPHASIS::function:: evaluates to CODE::true::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.select({ |n| n.midi >= 60 }); // Returns every item with MIDI value greater than or equal to 60
::



METHOD:: reject
Rejects every item of a collection, for which the EMPHASIS::function:: evaluates to CODE::true::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.reject({ |n| n.midi >= 60 }); // Returns every item with MIDI value lesser than 60
::



METHOD:: collect
Collects item from a collection based on the non-boolean evaluation of the EMPHASIS::function:: provided.

NOTE:: Contrary to CODE::select:: and CODE::reject::, which return a new MENoteRange object, CODE::collect:: returns a regular Array.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.collect({ |n| n.midi }); // Returns all MIDI values from each of the MEnotes
::



SUBSECTION:: Clip, wrap, fold and pyramid


METHOD:: clipAt
If MATH::index > (size - 1)::, CODE::clipAt:: will keep returning the last item.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r = r[25..30];
r.size;        // 6
r.clipAt(4);   // E6:m7
r.clipAt(5);   // F#6:P1
r.clipAt(6);   // F#6:P1
r.clipAt(7);   // F#6:P1
::




METHOD:: wrapAt
If MATH::index > (size - 1)::, CODE::wrapAt:: will keep counting back from the beginning, for the remaining positions.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r = r[25..30];
r.size;        // 6
r.wrapAt(4);   // E6:m7
r.wrapAt(5);   // F#6:P1
r.wrapAt(6);   // E5:m7
r.wrapAt(7);   // F#5:P1
::




METHOD:: foldAt
If MATH::index > (size - 1)::, CODE::foldAt:: will keep counting back from the end, for the remaining positions.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r = r[25..30];
r.size;        // 6
r.foldAt(4);   // E6:m7
r.foldAt(5);   // F#6:P1
r.foldAt(6);   // E6:m7
r.foldAt(7);   // C#6:P5
::



METHOD:: clipExtend
If EMPHASIS::index:: is greater than MATH::size - 1::, CODE::clipExtend:: will extend the collection by repeating the last item.

NOTE::
All repeated MENote objects have unique identities.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].clipExtend(10); // Last E5 gets repeated 5 times
::



METHOD:: wrapExtend
If EMPHASIS::index:: is greater than MATH::size - 1::, CODE::wrapExtend:: will extend the sequance by repeating items from the start.

NOTE::
All repeated MENote objects have unique identities.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].wrapExtend(10); // Last four items repeat the start of the sequence
::



METHOD:: foldExtend
if EMPHASIS::index:: is greater than MATH::size - 1::, CODE::foldExtend:: will extend the sequence by folding back from the last item.

NOTE::
All repeated MENote objects have unique identities.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r[20..25].foldExtend(10); // Sequence goes up to E5, then back down again to E4
::



METHOD:: pyramid
Returns new MENoteRange whose elements have been reordered via one of 10 "counting" algorithms. Run the examples to see the results. The argument EMPHASIS::patternType:: takes an integer up to 10.

NOTE::
CODE::pyramid:: returns a new MENoteRange. All repeated MENote objects have unique identities.
::

CODE::
(
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

10.do { |i|
	r[20..25].pyramid(i).postln;
};
)

c = r[20..25].pyramid(1);
c[0] === c[1] // false
::

SUBSECTION:: Operators

copymethod:: SequenceableCollection, -|@|

copymethod:: SequenceableCollection, -@@

copymethod:: SequenceableCollection, -@|@



METHOD:: ==
Comparison operator for equality.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");

a = r[20..30];
b = r[20..30];
a == b;        // Ranges a and b are equal

c = r[20..25];
a == c;        // Ranges a and c are not equal
::



copymethod:: Object, -===



SUBSECTION:: Indexing methods


METHOD:: firstIndexInOctave
Returns the index of the first MENote found with matching EMPHASIS::octave:: number. If EMPHASIS::octave:: MATH::> 9:: or MATH::< -1::, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE::
Middle EMPHASIS::C:: = EMPHASIS::C4:: = MIDI 60. Octaves go from -1 to 9.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.firstIndexInOctave(4);  // 20
r[20];                    // C#4
r.firstIndexInOctave(-2); // nil
::



METHOD:: lastIndexInOctave
Returns the index of the last MENote found with matching EMPHASIS::octave:: number. If EMPHASIS::octave:: MATH::> 9:: or MATH::< -1::, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE::
Middle EMPHASIS::C:: = EMPHASIS::C4:: = MIDI 60. Octaves go from -1 to 9.
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.lastIndexInOctave(4);  // 23
r[23];                   // A4
r.lastIndexInOctave(10); // nil
::



METHOD:: firstIndexOfDegree
Returns the index of the first MENote found with a matching EMPHASIS::degree::. If the EMPHASIS::degree:: provided is not present in the range, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.firstIndexOfDegree(\m7); // 1
r[1];                      // E-1:m7
r.firstIndexOfDegree(\P4); // Minor seventh chord does not have a P4 degree
::



METHOD:: lastIndexOfDegree
Returns the index of the last MENote found with a matching EMPHASIS::degree::. If the EMPHASIS::degree:: provided is not present in the range, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.lastIndexOfDegree(\m7); // 41
r[41];                    // E9:m7
r.lastIndexOfDegree(\P4); // Minor seventh chord does not have a P4 degree
::



METHOD:: firstIndexOfName
Returns the index of the first MENote found with matching EMPHASIS::name::. If the EMPHASIS::name:: provided is not present in the range, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.firstIndexOfName("F#"); // 2
r[2];                     // F#-1:P1
r.firstIndexOfName("F");  // Current range does not have F natural
::



METHOD:: lastIndexOfName
Returns the index of the last MENote found with matching EMPHASIS::name::. If the EMPHASIS::name:: provided is not present in the range, CODE::nil:: is returned.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.lastIndexOfName("F#"); // 42
r[42];                   // F#9:P1
r.lastIndexOfName("F");  // Current range does not have F natural
::



METHOD:: firstOverMIDI
Returns index of first MENote with MIDI value MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::midi::. if EMPHASIS::midi:: MATH::> 127::, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange("F#-7");
r.firstOverMIDI(66);  // 22
r[22];                // F#4:P1
r[22].midi;           // 66 is actually part of the range

r.firstOverMIDI(67);  // 23
r[23];                // A4:m3
r[23].midi;           // 69

r.firstOverMIDI(128); // nil
::


METHOD:: firstUnderMIDI
Returns index of first MENote with MIDI value MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::midi::. if EMPHASIS::midi:: MATH::< -1::, CODE::nil:: is returned.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.firstUnderMIDI(66); // 22
r[22];                // F#4:P1
r[22].midi;           // 66 is actually part of the range

r.firstUnderMIDI(65); // 21
r[21];                // E4:m7
r[21].midi;           // 64

r.firstUnderMIDI(-2); // nil
::



METHOD:: firstOverFreq
Returns index of first MENote with frequency value MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::freq::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.firstOverFreq(440); // 23
r[23];                // A4:m3
r[23].freq;           // 440Hz is actually part of the range

r.firstOverFreq(450); // 24
r[24];                // C#4:P5
r[24].freq;           // 554.36Hz
::


METHOD:: firstUnderFreq
Returns index of first MENote with frequency value MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::freq::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.firstUnderFreq(440); // 23
r[23];                 // A4:m3
r[23].freq;            // 440Hz is actually part of the range

r.firstUnderFreq(430); // 24
r[22];                 // F#4:P1
r[22].freq;            // 369.99Hz
::



METHOD:: degreeOverMIDI
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::degree::, and MIDI value MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::midi::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.degreeOverMIDI(\P1, 60); // 22
r[22];                     // F#4:P1
r[22].midi;                // 66
::


METHOD:: degreeUnderMIDI
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::degree::, and MIDI value MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::midi::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.degreeUnderMIDI(\P1, 60); // 18
r[18];                      // F#3:P1
r[18].midi;                 // 54
::


METHOD:: degreeOverFreq
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::degree::, and frequency value MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::freq::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.degreeOverFreq(\P5, 440); // 24
r[24];                      // C#5:P5
r[24].freq;                 // 554.36Hz
::


METHOD:: degreeUnderFreq
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::degree::, and frequency value MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::freq::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.degreeUnderFreq(\P5, 440); // 20
r[20];                       // C#4:P5
r[20].freq;                  // 227.18Hz
::


METHOD:: nameOverMIDI
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::name:: and MIDI value MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::midi::.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.nameOverMIDI("F#", 60); // 22
r[22];                    // F#4:P1
r[22].midi;               // 66
::


METHOD:: nameUnderMIDI
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::name:: and MIDI value MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::midi::.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.nameUnderMIDI("F#", 60); // 18
r[18];                     // F#3:P1
r[18].midi;                // 54
::



METHOD:: nameOverFreq
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::name::, and frequency value MATH::\ge:: EMPHASIS::freq::.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.nameOverFreq("C#", 440); // 24
r[24];                     // C#5:P5
r[24].freq;                // 554.36Hz
::



METHOD:: nameUnderFreq
Returns first instance of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::name::, and frequency value MATH::\le:: EMPHASIS::freq::.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.nameUnderFreq("C#", 440); // 20
r[20];                      // C#4:P5
r[20].freq;                 // 227.18Hz
::



METHOD:: degreeInOctave
Returns index of MENote with matching EMPHASIS::degree::, in respective EMPHASIS::octave::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.degreeInOctave(\m3, 4); // 23
r[23];                    // A4:m3
r[23].degree;             // m3
r[23].octave;             // 4
::



METHOD:: indicesOfDegree
Returns an Array containing indeces for all MENote objects with matching EMPHASIS::degree::.

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
i = r.indicesOfDegree(\P1); // [2, 6, 10, 14, 18, 22, 26, 30, 34, 38, 42]
i.do { |i| "% : %".format(r[i].degree, r[i].name).postln };
::



METHOD:: indicesOfName
Returns an Array containing indeces for all MENote objects with matching EMPHASIS::name::.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::without:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C"::, EMPHASIS::"F#"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
i = r.indicesOfName("C#"); // [0, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 36, 40]
i.do { |i| "% : %".format(r[i].degree, r[i].name).postln };
::



METHOD:: indexOfName
Takes a CODE::String:: describing the note name, with an appending octave number, and returns the corresponding index.

NOTE:: This method requires a note name STRONG::with:: an octave number (e.g.: EMPHASIS::"C4"::, EMPHASIS::"F#5"::, etc.).
::

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
r.indexOfName("C#4"); // 20
r[20];                // C#4:P5
::
